    "summary": "Programming language used in many domains In computer software , a general-purpose programming language ( GPL ) is a programming language for building software in a wide variety of application domains . Conversely, a domain-specific programming language (DSL) is used within a specific area. For example, Python is a GPL, while SQL is a DSL for querying relational databases .",
